.TH DSH-DESKTOP 1 "September 2026" "dsh-desktop 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dsh-desktop \- native desktop launcher for DeepSeek Harness
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dsh-desktop
[\fB\-\-url=\fR\fIURL\fR]
[\fB\-\-ozone-platform-hint=\fR\fImode\fR]
[\fB\-\-daemon\fR | \fB\-\-foreground\fR]
[\fIOPTIONS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBdsh-desktop\fR is the native desktop launcher and sandboxed Electron frontend
for DeepSeek Harness (@deepseek-ai/dsh).
.PP
On invocation, \fBdsh-desktop\fR ensures that the background runtime service is
running (starting \fIdsh-desktop.service\fR via \fBsystemctl\fR(1) or falling back
to launching a background daemon), discovers the loopback port bound by the harness,
and launches the application window. If an Electron environment is not available,
it falls back to running supported browsers in application mode or opening the URL
via \fBxdg-open\fR(1).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-url=\fR\fIURL\fR
Override the target URL to display in the desktop window instead of waiting
for and discovering the local harness service.
.TP
\fB\-\-ozone-platform-hint=\fR\fImode\fR
Configure the Ozone platform abstraction layer for Chromium/Electron. Defaults
to \fBauto\fR to automatically negotiate native Wayland or X11 display servers.
.TP
\fB\-\-daemon\fR
Execute the DeepSeek Harness server entry script directly in the foreground
without launching the desktop user interface.
.TP
\fB\-\-foreground\fR
Alias for \fB\-\-daemon\fR.
.TP
\fIOPTIONS\fR
Additional options are passed directly to the underlying Electron application.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DSH_HOME
Base directory for DeepSeek Harness state, user profiles, and installed
plugins. When unset or empty, defaults to \fI~/.dsh\fR.
.TP
.B DSH_URL
Fallback target URL when no running harness instance can be discovered from
logs or open loopback ports. Defaults to \fIhttp://127.0.0.1:3080\fR.
.TP
.B XDG_SESSION_TYPE
Identifies the display server protocol (\fIwayland\fR or \fIx11\fR), used
by Electron and the Ozone platform layer to enable native Wayland rendering
and hardware acceleration.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.dsh/
User runtime directory holding configuration, profiles, and plugins.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/dsh-desktop/
System installation directory containing the launcher, daemon executable,
and package helper binaries.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/dsh-desktop/dsh.log
Default log file for harness daemon output and diagnostics.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dsh-desktop-daemon (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
